  "notes": [
    "DRAFT: a raid plan written offline in task B1 (TortoiseBots-audit RAID-PREP-bwl.md) from the world database export of map 469 (284 creature spawns, 27 entries, 91 game objects; sql/base 2026-09-12), the core's blackwing_lair instance and boss scripts and the server's map 469 navmesh (16 tiles). Not mapped, not live-checked: the GM-invisible mapping walk (B2) and the first live run are still to do; dungeon_run refuses it without allow_draft.",
    "Packs: the draft's 64 pull groups (275 units) become 43 pull groups of 273 units: the two Tortured Drakes (13976, neutral, level 40) and Master Elemental Shaper Krixix (14401, gossip flag) are in no pull, and the rest are chained where they stand within 15 yd on one floor (|dz| \u003c= 4) and where the walk from one to the next is no longer than 2.2 times their distance plus 8 yd. The merge stops when a pack's own radius would pass 18 yd: the Suppression Room is a uniform field of 158 spawns (134 whelps of four colours, 12 hatchers, 12 taskmasters) 8-14 yd apart, so the 15-yd chain alone takes 16 units across 54 yd (radius 26.9). Each group's radius is its own spread from its centre plus 0.5, kept inside the nearest spawn of every entry it lists (1.7 to 17.9 yd).",
    "The instance keeps every non-GM player inside Razorgore's room until TYPE_RAZORGORE is DONE: instance_blackwing_lair.cpp Update teleports a player farther than 100 yd from razorgoreRoomCenter (-7596.10 -1053.41 408.15) or above z 420 back to the room (\"Cheating detected. Cannot leave boss room before encounter is complete.\"). Legs 1 to 7 lie past that line, so a headless run cannot reach Vaelastrasz or any later boss before the Razorgore encounter is completed.",
    "Razorgore's encounter needs a player at the Orb of Domination (177808 at -7615.05 -1026.24 413.381): GOHello_go_orbe_domination possesses Razorgore only when he is already in combat, and the 30 Black Dragon Eggs (177807) are destroyed only by the possessed Razorgore (go_oeuf_razAI OnUse). The plan pulls Grethok the Controller (12557) and his two Blackwing Guardsmen, whose enter-combat starts the event, then fights Razorgore; it has no orb or egg step because no bot can take the orb. Blocker, see the prep.",
    "Vaelastrasz (13020) and Lord Victor Nefarius (10162) are started by a gossip chain of two and three menus: each selection shows the next menu, and the run leader's gossip step sends one hello and one select, so it reaches the first menu only. The plan writes the first level and makes each boss the event's hold on its instance data (1 and 7); both are blockers until the run can chain gossip options or a player talks.",
    "Doors: the eight Portcullis doors (176964/176965/179364/179365/179115/179116/179117/176966) start open (the spawn state and the template's startOpen agree), the lever 179148 has no script in the core, and the instance opens the doors on each boss's DONE. No door, lever or key gates the route, so the plan has no wait_object or use_object step.",
    "Suppression Room: 38 Suppression Devices (179784) apply Suppression (22247) within 15 yd of every non-stealthed, non-GM player, and are deleted once Broodlord Lashlayer is DONE (go_engin_suppressionAI, instance OnObjectCreate); the bots' own strategy disarms them (disarm suppression device, BlackwingLairDungeonStrategies.cpp), so the plan has no step for them.",
    "Patrols: no map 469 spawn has a waypoint path (creature_movement has no point for any of the 284 guids; the movement type 2 spawns have no path), so no pull group carries a patrol block and there is no estimated period for the walk to measure.",
    "Boss order: Razorgore, Vaelastrasz, Broodlord Lashlayer, Firemaw, Ebonroc, Flamegor, Chromaggus, Nefarian (the instance loads the later bosses only once Razorgore is DONE, and each door opens on the boss before it). Nefarian (11583) has no world spawn: Lord Victor Nefarius summons him at 40 killed adds and he lands at -7495.96 -1252.40 476.80, which is the boss row's position.",
    "No ai_boss_tactic rows: the eight bosses cast from C++ and the bots' own Blackwing Lair strategies already cover the front cone, the drakes' facing, the Flame Buffet stacks, the Chromaggus afflictions and the Nefarian class calls (dungeons-and-raids.md); the trash casters (Spellbinder Greater Polymorph 22274, Hatcher Flamestrike 22275, Warlock Rain of Fire 19717 and Demon Portal 22372, Wyrmkin Blast Wave 22424) are not bosses and their interrupts are the bot AI's current-target interrupts. A 'behind' row would duplicate the raid positioning the bot AI already does.",
    "Community: waterys419 has no Blackwing Lair report. The inventory's per-boss patches would be Razorgore 309, Vaelastrasz 310, Ebonroc 258 and Nefarian 311/312/313/316; none is needed by this data and none is cherry-picked (owner decision)."
  ],
